![an illustration of fun trivia questions and answers](https://formester-strapi.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/trivia_788c203a95.png)

A funny trivia quiz is the cheapest icebreaker that consistently works. [TeamOut's 2025 workplace games review](https://www.teamout.com/blog-post/trivia-questions-for-work) and [Event Gamification's 2025 report](https://eventgamification.com/team-trivia/) both put trivia in the top five team-building activities for remote and hybrid teams. 

The friction is finding 100 questions that are actually funny, not just "name the capital of Bolivia" recycled across ten blog posts. That's what this page is for.

You'll find 100 questions across ten categories below, organised so you can copy the ones that fit your crowd. 

There's also a playable Formester quiz you can send via Slack, Teams, WhatsApp, or email in 90 seconds.

Want to spin up your own trivia quiz from scratch? Formester's [AI form generator](/ai-form-generator/) turns a single sentence ("a 10-question movie trivia quiz with multiple-choice answers and a scored result") into a live, shareable quiz in under 30 seconds. 

And four themed variants for the situations people actually run trivia in: adult parties, kids, work meetings, and Christmas.

